                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15745271" author="isapego" created="Tue, 13 Dec 2016 14:19:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I found a root cause of the issue. In &lt;tt&gt;OdbcRequestHandler&lt;/tt&gt; we now acquire keep-binary cache instance (&lt;tt&gt;withKeepBinary()&lt;/tt&gt;), so any complex object returned as an instance of  &lt;tt&gt;BinaryObjectExImpl&lt;/tt&gt;, which serialized as &lt;tt&gt;IGNITE_TYPE_BINARY&lt;/tt&gt;. Currently, we don&apos;t handle objects of type &lt;tt&gt;IGNITE_TYPE_BINARY&lt;/tt&gt; in ODBC driver.&lt;br/&gt;
I&apos;m going to implement it.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
